% KSSstep - performs one time step of a KSS method for solving
% P_t + LP = 0, on a Chebyshev grid, where
% LP = -a2 P_XX + a1 P_X + a0 P.
%
% This function implements a KSS method via a physical-space polynomial 
% evaluation. This approach applies a different polynomial approximation 
% of the solution operator, exp(-J*dt), to each point in the solution 
% vector directly.
%
% The frequency-dependent coefficients for each polynomial are pre-computed
% by the 'getslopes' function. The polynomial is then applied to the 
% solution vector and its derivatives (LP, L2P) using element-wise vector
% multiplication.
%
% input:
% P     - solution from the previous time step.
% dT    - the time step.
% a0    - coefficient vector.
% a1    - coefficient vector.
% a2    - coefficient vector.
% D1    - first Chebyshev derivative matrix.
% D2    - second Chebyshev derivative matrix.
% ord   - order of accuracy in time.
%
% output:
% P - solution at the new time.
function P = KSSstep(P,dT,a0,a1,a2,D1,D2,ord)

% Compute the 3xN matrix of frequency-dependent polynomial coefficients
coeffs = getslopes(dT, ord, a0, a2);  

% Apply the operator L once to get LP = L*P
LP  = applyop(P, a0, a1, a2, D1, D2);

% Apply the operator L a second time to get L2P = L*(L*P)
L2P = applyop(LP, a0, a1, a2, D1, D2);

% Apply the polynomial to the vectors P, LP and L2P 
if ord == 2
   % Extract coefficients for c0, c1, and c2 as column vectors
   c0 = coeffs(1,:)';   c1 = coeffs(2,:)';   c2 = coeffs(3,:)';

   %Evalute the second-ord polynomial in the physical space
   P = c0.*P + c1.*LP + c2.*L2P;
else
  c0 = coeffs(1,:)';   c1 = coeffs(2,:)';
  P = c0.*P + c1.*LP;
end
